{"text": "Jamie\n\nTopsfield, MA\n\n(202) 642-4959\n\n=\nelsito rn\n\nProfile\n\nAchievements:\n\nExperience\n\nEducation\n\nWebsite:\nbelsitoforcongress.com\n\nDemocratic Candidate for the Sixth Congressional District. Mother, progressive leader,\n\u2018education activist, mental health advocate, policy expert, women's rights champion, wife.\n\n\u2018Advocated on Capitol Hill for the Successful Passage of the Following Bils:\nH.R. 1318: \u201cPreventing Maternal Deaths Act of 2018\"\nH.R. 3235: Congresswoman Katherine Clark's \"Bringing Postpartum Depression Out of the\n\u2018Shadows Act of 2015\" [21st Century Cures Act]\nH.R. 5291: \"Safe Medications for Moms and Babies Act\u201d\nH.R. 5065: \"BABES Act\u201d Bottles and Breastfeeding Equipment Screening Act\n\u2018American Competitiveness and Workforce Improvement Act\n\u2018American Competitiveness in the 21 Century Act\n\u2018Spousal Work Permits for L1 Visa Holders\n\nFounder, Maternal Mental Health Leadership Alliance - 2018-Present\nCreated the only advocacy organization in the nation dedicated to achieving positive maternal\n\u2018mental health policies on Capital Hill. Ended TSA's rules on disposing breast milk on flights.\n\u2018Made postpartum care part of the ACA. Got funding for states to study why women of color\ndie at disproportionately high levels during childbirth in this nation.\n\nHR Executive, 2001-2006, 2008-2009\nLed immigration programs and international deployment initiatives for major international\ncompanies, including: AOL, Raytheon, and Philips.\n\nFederal lobbyist, American Council on International Personnel ~ 2006-2008\nPartnered with coalitions to craft business immigration reform and legislation.\nWorked with Senator Ted Kennedy's office to formulate the H-181 Visa Program, spousal\n\u2018work permit opportunities, and American workforce retraining programs.\n\nCongressional Intern, Congressman Joe Moakley ~ 1996-1997\nFacilitated immigration cases for families in the district who wanted their loved ones to be\nreunited in this country. Helped reduce the district's 20-year backlog of cases.\n\nSalem State College - BA, political science 1996\nReading Memorial High School \u2014 1991",
